WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:10.264
These companies race each other every day. For customers, for talent, for chips.

2
00:00:10.644 --> 00:00:13.664
So why would they sign the same promise?

3
00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:21.864
One reason is shared risk. If one company gets it badly wrong, trust in the whole industry can suffer.

4
00:00:22.804 --> 00:00:32.584
Another is timing. Congress has not passed national SI safety rules, so a common set of steps gives industry and Washington a starting point.

5
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:38.024
Mark Zuckerberg called it a start: “an accord that the whole industry could come to.”

6
00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:50.984
Critics see another motive. A voluntary pledge can head off tougher, binding rules. Former FTC chair Lina Khan said self-regulation by big tech has been “a proven failure.”

7
00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:57.784
Either way, fierce rivals put their names on the same page. That doesn't happen often.
